TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Orbit Specifics"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – STK Design & Simulations"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Background Research"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – final paragraph"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Orbit Specifics","issue":"A geostationary orbit is at about 35,786 km, not 600 km (600 km is LEO). A GEO satellite also sits over the equator, so it cannot remain fixed above the reef at about 10–24°S."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Editing & Finalisation vs Image 1","issue":"The text reserves weeks 7 and 8 for editing and finalisation, but the Gantt chart schedules Editing & Finalisation in weeks 9 and 10."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The communications and near-real-time relay requirement is not linked to any orbit, link budget or ground-station design, so the space segment is not related to the mission function."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Launch Specifics","issue":"Launch vehicle, trajectory and site are listed as tasks but no preliminary launch or orbit analysis is presented to support them."}],"overall":"Clear mission motivation with good referencing, but the stated geostationary 600 km orbit is physically incorrect and undermines the concept. The plan has a schedule inconsistency and no explicit contingencies. Preliminary technical results are absent, and the software and information sources are only implicit.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":20.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Motivation and purpose are clear, with bleaching monitoring, near-real-time relay and scientist users, and footnoted sources. However, goals and requirements are not quantified (resolution, revisit, coverage, lifetime), wider Australian beneficiaries are thin, and the stated orbit contradicts the mission function. This sits in the Adequate range.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Orbit Specifics","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km, which keeps the satellite fixed above the reef at all times."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":15.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A week-based Gantt chart with status colours and deadlines is provided and the plan appears feasible. There is no explicit contingency or variation provision, and the task text conflicts with the chart on editing weeks. Information sources are only implicit in the plan and are not justified within the mission narrative, placing it in the Adequate range.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Strategies","quote":"gradually cut and refine them over the next few weeks"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Editing & Finalisation","quote":"Weeks 7 and 8 are reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Some work has been completed: background reading, the Asner brief and STK tutorials. No technical results are shown, such as orbit calculations, COE/AOE values, STK screenshots or hand calculations, and there is no interpretation. Progress is minor rather than demonstrated, placing it at the lower end of Adequate.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – final paragraph","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Headings and superscript citations matching footnotes are used, and writing is mostly clear. The Gantt chart has no figure caption, bare-URL footnotes lack source details, and the notes-style bullets ('Need to decide', 'More STK simulations needed') are informal. Section titles are inconsistent, so this is upper Adequate.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – End of Life","quote":"Need to decide how to dispose/recycle the satellite after its lifespan"},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""}]}]}
